Q: Export plotly to powerpoint in R A: <p>Powerpoint is no webviewer. Thus implementing a Plotly.js chart that bases on d3.js as interactive plot is very very tricky. I struggle to find a proper usecase for this and would recommend to just create a presentation using Quarto, Flexdashboard, Reveal.js or similar. Still, here is a way:</p>
<ol>
<li>Go to <a href="https://github.com/" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><code>github.com</code></a> -&gt; New repository -&gt; call it e.g. &quot;plotly-addin&quot;</li>
<li>Create a file called <code>index.html</code> with this content. This basically let's the user enter any address and then sets the iframes' source to that.</li>
</ol>
<pre><code>&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;
&lt;html&gt;
&lt;head&gt;
  &lt;meta charset=&quot;UTF-8&quot; /&gt;
  &lt;title&gt;Web Viewer&lt;/title&gt;
  &lt;script src=&quot;https://appsforoffice.microsoft.com/lib/1/hosted/office.js&quot;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;
  &lt;style&gt;
    * { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }
    body { font-family: Segoe UI, sans-serif; display: flex; flex-direction: column; height: 100vh; padding: 8px; gap: 8px; }
    .controls { display: flex; gap: 6px; }
    input {
      flex: 1; padding: 6px 10px; border: 1px solid #ccc;
      border-radius: 4px; font-size: 13px;
    }
    button {
      padding: 6px 14px; background: #0078d4; color: white;
      border: none; border-radius: 4px; cursor: pointer; font-size: 13px;
    }
    button:hover { background: #106ebe; }
    iframe { flex: 1; border: 1px solid #eee; border-radius: 4px; width: 100%; }
  &lt;/style&gt;
&lt;/head&gt;
&lt;body&gt;
  &lt;div class=&quot;controls&quot;&gt;
    &lt;input type=&quot;url&quot; id=&quot;urlInput&quot; placeholder=&quot;http://...&quot; /&gt;
    &lt;button onclick=&quot;loadUrl()&quot;&gt;Load&lt;/button&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;iframe id=&quot;viewer&quot; sandbox=&quot;allow-scripts allow-same-origin allow-forms&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;

  &lt;script&gt;
    Office.onReady(() =&gt; {});

    function loadUrl() {
      const url = document.getElementById(&quot;urlInput&quot;).value.trim();
      document.getElementById(&quot;viewer&quot;).src = url;
    }
  &lt;/script&gt;
&lt;/body&gt;
&lt;/html&gt;
</code></pre>
<ol start="3">
<li>Go to Settings and Pages in your repo, set &quot;branch&quot; to main branch and Save.</li>
</ol>
<p><a href="https://i.sstatic.net/TOsAfFJj.png" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><img src="https://i.sstatic.net/TOsAfFJj.png" alt="res" /></a></p>
<p>--&gt; GitHub gives you a URL &quot;Your site is live at:&quot; <a href="https://yourusername.github.io/plotly-addin/" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://yourusername.github.io/plotly-addin/</a></p>
<ol start="4">
<li>Create a <code>manifest.xml</code> file in folder <code>C:\ppt_manifest\</code>. Herein set SourceLocation as your github-link.</li>
</ol>
<pre><code>&lt;?xml version=&quot;1.0&quot; encoding=&quot;UTF-8&quot;?&gt;
&lt;OfficeApp xmlns=&quot;http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/appforoffice/1.1&quot;
           xmlns:xsi=&quot;http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance&quot;
           xsi:type=&quot;TaskPaneApp&quot;&gt;
  &lt;Id&gt;d1919f0a-3d6a-44d7-8d64-e8328ca9531a&lt;/Id&gt;
  &lt;Version&gt;1.0.0.0&lt;/Version&gt;
  &lt;ProviderName&gt;You&lt;/ProviderName&gt;
  &lt;DefaultLocale&gt;en-US&lt;/DefaultLocale&gt;
  &lt;DisplayName DefaultValue=&quot;Web Viewer&quot; /&gt;
  &lt;Description DefaultValue=&quot;View any http URL in task pane&quot; /&gt;
  &lt;Hosts&gt;
    &lt;Host Name=&quot;Presentation&quot; /&gt;
  &lt;/Hosts&gt;
  &lt;DefaultSettings&gt;
    &lt;SourceLocation DefaultValue=&quot;https://yourusername.github.io/plotly-addin/&quot; /&gt;
  &lt;/DefaultSettings&gt;
  &lt;Permissions&gt;ReadWriteDocument&lt;/Permissions&gt;
&lt;/OfficeApp&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>Right-click the <code>C:\ppt_manifest\</code> folder -&gt; Properties -&gt; Sharing -&gt; Share it and note the network path it gives you, i.e. <code>\\DESKTOP-0U5B5UM\ppt_manifest</code>.</p>
<p><strong>In PowerPoint:</strong> Options -&gt; Trust Center  -&gt; Trust Center Settings  -&gt; Trusted Add-in Catalogs. Paste the <code>\\DESKTOP-0U5B5UM\ppt_manifest</code> path -&gt; Add Catalog -&gt; check &quot;Show in Menu&quot; -&gt; OK.
<a href="https://i.sstatic.net/Da51Ah24.png" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><img src="https://i.sstatic.net/Da51Ah24.png" alt="add network path to trustnetwork" /></a>
6. Restart PowerPoint.
7. Finally open your Add-In: Developer -&gt; Add-Ins -&gt; Shared Folder -&gt; &quot;Web Viewer&quot;
<a href="https://i.sstatic.net/w8U2AuY8.png" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><img src="https://i.sstatic.net/w8U2AuY8.png" alt="enter image description here" /></a></p>
<ol start="8">
<li>In R, serve your plotly on a server</li>
</ol>
<pre><code>library(plotly)
library(htmlwidgets)
library(servr)  # install.packages(&quot;servr&quot;)

p &lt;- plot_ly(mtcars, x = ~wt, y = ~mpg, type = &quot;scatter&quot;, mode = &quot;markers&quot;)
saveWidget(p, &quot;D:/Dokumente/R/Plotly in Powerpoint/chart.html&quot;, selfcontained = TRUE)

servr::httd(&quot;D:/Dokumente/R/Plotly in Powerpoint&quot;) # Serve the folder on localhost

# To stop the server, run servr::daemon_stop(1) or restart your R session
# Serving the directory D:\Dokumente\R\Plotly in Powerpoint at http://127.0.0.1:4321
</code></pre>
<p>Copy the address &quot;http://127.0.0.1:4321&quot; into the powerpoint Add-In and navigate to the plotly chart!</p>
<p><a href="https://i.sstatic.net/3KPtScpl.gif" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><img src="https://i.sstatic.net/3KPtScpl.gif" alt="res" /></a></p>
<hr />
<ul>
<li>If you know, you serve &quot;http://127.0.0.1:4321&quot;, consider updating the <code>index.html</code> with a hardcoded URL</li>
<li>To host a shiny app, link to &quot;Listening on ...&quot; e.g.:</li>
</ul>
<p><a href="https://i.sstatic.net/trmfXlQy.png" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><img src="https://i.sstatic.net/trmfXlQy.png" alt="res" /></a></p>
<p>I hope this works for you.</p>

Q: NavigationStack within a NavigationSplitView show unexpected behavior A: <p>The inspector remains present if you attach it to the parent <code>NavigationSplitView</code>, instead of to the nested <code>NavigationStack</code>. This means moving the state variable to the parent and passing it as a binding to <code>Page2View</code>.</p>
<p>You might also want to reset the flag when the top-level navigation changes away from <code>.page2</code>. One way to do this is to add an <code>.onDisappear</code> closure to <code>Page2View</code>.</p>
<pre class="lang-swift prettyprint-override"><code>// MainView

@State private var showsInspector: Bool = false // 👈 moved to MainView

// ...

var body: some View {
    NavigationSplitView {
        // ...
    } detail: {
        switch selectedPage {
        case .page1:
            Page1View()
        case .page2:
            Page2View(showsInspector: $showsInspector) // 👈 pass flag as binding
        case nil:
            Text(&quot;Select a page&quot;)
        }
    }
    .inspector(isPresented: $showsInspector) { // 👈 attach inspector here
        Text(&quot;Inspector&quot;)
    }
}
</code></pre>
<pre class="lang-swift prettyprint-override"><code>struct Page2View: View {
    @Binding var showsInspector: Bool // 👈 @State changed to @Binding

    var body: some View {
        NavigationStack {
            Page2ContentView(folderName: &quot;Main&quot;)
        }
        // 👈 inspector removed
        .toolbar {
            Button {
                showsInspector.toggle()
            } label: {
                Image(systemName: &quot;sidebar.right&quot;)
            }
        }
        .onDisappear { 👈 added
            showsInspector = false
        }
    }
}
</code></pre>
<p><img src="https://i.sstatic.net/kZ9c0orb.gif" alt="Animation" /></p>
<p>You will notice that the button disappears when navigating to the nested folder view. A workaround here is to move the <code>.toolbar</code> modifier from <code>Page2View</code> to <code>Page2ContentView</code> and pass on the binding to this view too.</p>
<p>Of course, if you want to display information in the inspector that depends on the nested context then this would need to be passed back to the parent via a binding in the same way.</p>
